public class ContactTriggerHandler {

    public static void execute() {
        if (Trigger.isBefore) {
            handleBefore();
        }
        if (Trigger.isAfter && Trigger.isInsert) {
            handleAfterInsert();
        }
    }

    private static void handleBefore() {
        Set<Id> accountIds = new Set<Id>();
        for (Contact c : Trigger.new) {
            if (c.AccountId != null) {
                accountIds.add(c.AccountId);
            }
        }

        if (accountIds.isEmpty()) {
            return;
        }

        // 1 SOQL query
        Map<Id, Account> accountMap = new Map<Id, Account>(
            [SELECT BillingCountry, AccountSource FROM Account WHERE Id IN :accountIds]
        );

        for (Contact c : Trigger.new) {
            if (c.AccountId != null) {
                Account a = accountMap.get(c.AccountId);
                if (a != null) {
                    if (String.isBlank(c.MailingCountry)) {
                        c.MailingCountry = a.BillingCountry;
                    }
                    if (Trigger.isInsert && String.isBlank(c.LeadSource)) {
                        c.LeadSource = a.AccountSource;
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }

    private static void handleAfterInsert() {
        // Group contacts by AccountId, preserving trigger-new order
        Map<Id, List<Contact>> contactsByAccount = new Map<Id, List<Contact>>();
        for (Contact c : Trigger.new) {
            if (c.AccountId != null && String.isNotBlank(c.Phone)) {
                if (!contactsByAccount.containsKey(c.AccountId)) {
                    contactsByAccount.put(c.AccountId, new List<Contact>());
                }
                contactsByAccount.get(c.AccountId).add(c);
            }
        }

        if (contactsByAccount.isEmpty()) {
            return;
        }

        // 1 SOQL query
        Map<Id, Account> accountMap = new Map<Id, Account>(
            [SELECT Id, Phone FROM Account WHERE Id IN :contactsByAccount.keySet()]
        );

        // Only accounts that currently have no phone get updated;
        // the first contact (in Trigger.new order) supplies the phone.
        List<Account> accountsToUpdate = new List<Account>();
        for (Id accountId : contactsByAccount.keySet()) {
            Account a = accountMap.get(accountId);
            if (a != null && String.isBlank(a.Phone)) {
                a.Phone = contactsByAccount.get(accountId).get(0).Phone;
                accountsToUpdate.add(a);
            }
        }

        // 1 DML statement
        if (!accountsToUpdate.isEmpty()) {
            update accountsToUpdate;
        }
    }
}
```

**Summary of the refactor and how the budget is met:**

| Context | SOQL queries | DML |
|---|---|---|
| Before (insert or update) | 1 (`SELECT … WHERE Id IN :accountIds`) | 0 |
| After insert | 1 (`SELECT … WHERE Id IN :contactsByAccount.keySet()`) | 1 (`update accountsToUpdate`) |
| **Total** | **2** | **1** |

**Key behavioural details preserved:**

* **Before context** – MailingCountry is back-filled from `BillingCountry` whenever the contact's field is blank; LeadSource is back-filled from `AccountSource` only on insert when the contact's field is blank. The account is fetched once per unique AccountId instead of once per contact.

* **After-insert "first-contact-wins" rule** – Contacts are grouped by AccountId while iterating `Trigger.new` in order. For each account whose `Phone` is currently blank, only the **first** contact in that group (index 0 of the list) supplies the phone value. Subsequent contacts for the same account are ignored, exactly matching the original loop's behaviour (where the second contact's fresh SOQL would see the already-updated phone and skip).

* **No queries or DML in the trigger itself** – the trigger body is a single delegate call; all logic lives in `ContactTriggerHandler`.

