public class OpportunityPipelineHandler {

    public static void handleInsert() {
        Set<Id> accountIds = collectAccountIds(Trigger.new);
        recalculate(accountIds);
    }

    public static void handleUpdate() {
        Set<Id> accountIds = new Set<Id>();
        for (Integer i = 0; i < Trigger.new.size(); i++) {
            Opportunity oldOpp = Trigger.old.get(i);
            Opportunity newOpp = Trigger.new.get(i);

            // Only recalculate when a field that affects the totals actually changed.
            // This also prevents re-entrant processing when the Account trigger
            // updates opportunities (it only sets FB_Account_Rating__c).
            if (oldOpp.Amount != newOpp.Amount
                    || oldOpp.IsClosed != newOpp.IsClosed
                    || oldOpp.AccountId != newOpp.AccountId) {
                if (oldOpp.AccountId != null) {
                    accountIds.add(oldOpp.AccountId);
                }
                if (newOpp.AccountId != null) {
                    accountIds.add(newOpp.AccountId);
                }
            }
        }
        recalculate(accountIds);
    }

    public static void handleDelete() {
        Set<Id> accountIds = collectAccountIds(Trigger.old);
        recalculate(accountIds);
    }

    public static void handleUndelete() {
        Set<Id> accountIds = collectAccountIds(Trigger.new);
        recalculate(accountIds);
    }

    // ------------------------------------------------------------------
    //  Core recalculation: re-read the current open pipeline from the
    //  database (SOQL within the same transaction sees all prior DML),
    //  then write the correct totals back to the affected accounts.
    // ------------------------------------------------------------------
    private static void recalculate(Set<Id> accountIds) {
        if (accountIds.isEmpty()) {
            return;
        }

        // Query the live open opportunities for every affected account.
        // Blank amounts are treated as 0.
        List<Opportunity> openOpps = [
            SELECT Id, AccountId, Amount
            FROM Opportunity
            WHERE AccountId IN :accountIds AND IsClosed = false
        ];

        // Initialise to 0 so accounts with no remaining open opps get 0, not blank.
        Map<Id, Decimal> pipelineMap = new Map<Id, Decimal>();
        Map<Id, Integer> countMap = new Map<Id, Integer>();
        for (Id accId : accountIds) {
            pipelineMap.put(accId, 0);
            countMap.put(accId, 0);
        }

        for (Opportunity o : openOpps) {
            pipelineMap.put(o.AccountId,
                pipelineMap.get(o.AccountId) + (o.Amount == null ? 0 : o.Amount));
            countMap.put(o.AccountId, countMap.get(o.AccountId) + 1);
        }

        List<Account> accountsToUpdate = new List<Account>();
        for (Id accId : accountIds) {
            Account acc = new Account(Id = accId);
            acc.FB_Open_Pipeline__c      = pipelineMap.get(accId);
            acc.FB_Open_Opportunities__c = countMap.get(accId);
            accountsToUpdate.add(acc);
        }

        update accountsToUpdate;
    }

    private static Set<Id> collectAccountIds(List<Opportunity> opps) {
        Set<Id> accountIds = new Set<Id>();
        for (Opportunity o : opps) {
            if (o.AccountId != null) {
                accountIds.add(o.AccountId);
            }
        }
        return accountIds;
    }
}
```

**How it works and why it is safe:**

| Concern | Handling |
|---|---|
| **Correctness after every DML** | Every trigger invocation performs a full re-query of open opportunities for the affected accounts. Because SOQL in the same transaction sees all prior DML, the totals are always a true snapshot of the current state. |
| **Multiple DML statements in one transaction** | Each statement re-fires the trigger; the recalculation reads the cumulative state, so the final numbers are always correct. No incremental arithmetic that could drift. |
| **Re-entrancy with the existing `AccountTrigger`** | Updating Account fires `AccountTrigger` (after update), which updates Opportunities (setting only `FB_Account_Rating__c`). That re-fires `OpportunityTrigger` → `handleUpdate`. The field-change guard (`Amount`, `IsClosed`, `AccountId`) detects that none of the relevant fields changed, so the second call is a no-op. The loop terminates after one extra cycle. |
| **Bulk / 200-record loads** | One SOQL (bounded by the number of open opps for the affected accounts) and one DML (bounded by the number of distinct accounts). All record iteration is in `for` loops over collections; no per-record SOQL or DML. |
| **Move to another account** | Both `oldOpp.AccountId` and `newOpp.AccountId` are added to the affected set, so both accounts get recalculated. |
| **0 instead of blank** | The maps are pre-seeded with `0` for every affected account before aggregation, so an account whose last open opportunity is removed gets `0` / `0`. |
| **Blank Amount counts as 0** | `(o.Amount == null ? 0 : o.Amount)` in the sum. |

