while (rangeStart > Date.valueOf(1990, 1, 1)) {
    Date rangeEnd = rangeStart;
    rangeStart = rangeStart.addDays(-7);
    // query WHERE CloseDate < :rangeEnd AND CloseDate >= :rangeStart …
}
```

or, for truly unbounded volume, move to a `Database.batchable` class. For the stated "few thousand" scale the simple for-loop is the right trade-off—less code, synchronous, easy to reason about, and well within every governor limit.

## StaleOpportunityCloser

The code below uses the list-form SOQL for-loop so the platform hands back at most 200 rows per iteration; each chunk is mutated and DML'd inside the loop, so we never hold more than one chunk in memory.

```apex
