## Summary of fixes

| Bug | Root cause | Fix |
|-----|-----------|-----|
| Added tasks don't appear | `this.items = this.tasks` shared the parent's array reference; `push` mutated in-place without a new assignment, so LWC's reactivity didn't re-render | `items` is now a **private copy** managed by the `tasks` setter; `handleAdd` reassigns `this.items = [...this.items, newTask]` to trigger reactivity |
| Toggling doesn't update counter / throws error | `task.done = !task.done` mutated the object in place (no re-render) and `find` compared a numeric `id` against a string `dataset.id`, returning `undefined` → crash | `handleToggle` reassigns the whole array via `.map`, comparing `String(task.id) === id` |
| Heading ignores later changes | `connectedCallback` overwrote `@api heading` with the upper-cased string, so the parent's original value was lost and subsequent parent updates were clobbered | Heading is never mutated; a **getter** (`displayHeading`) upper-cases on read |
| Parent never hears about new tasks | Event name was `'taskAdded'` (wrong case), `detail.label` was read *after* `newLabel` was cleared (always `''`), and `bubbles`/`composed` were missing | Dispatch `'taskadded'` with the trimmed label captured before clearing, `bubbles: true, composed: true` |
| Parent array / objects could be mutated | Direct reference to parent's array and task objects | `tasks` setter deep-copies both the array and each task object; all mutations happen on the private `items` copy |

