public class GauAllocationService {

    public class AllocationException extends Exception {}

    public static List<npsp__Allocation__c> allocateByPercent(Id opportunityId, Map<Id, Decimal> percentByGauId) {
        // --- Validation (before any DML) ---

        if (percentByGauId == null || percentByGauId.isEmpty()) {
            throw new AllocationException('Allocation map cannot be null or empty.');
        }

        // Check each percentage value and accumulate the total
        Decimal totalPercent = 0;
        for (Id gauId : percentByGauId.keySet()) {
            Decimal pct = percentByGauId.get(gauId);
            if (pct == null || pct <= 0) {
                throw new AllocationException(
                    'Percentages must be greater than 0. Invalid value for GAU ' + gauId + '.'
                );
            }
            totalPercent += pct;
        }

        if (totalPercent > 100) {
            throw new AllocationException(
                'Percentages cannot total more than 100%. Received total: ' + totalPercent + '%.'
            );
        }

        // Verify all referenced GAUs exist and are active
        Set<Id> gauIds = percentByGauId.keySet();
        Map<Id, npsp__General_Accounting_Unit__c> gauMap =
            new Map<Id, npsp__General_Accounting_Unit__c>(
                [SELECT Id, Name, npsp__Active__c
                 FROM npsp__General_Accounting_Unit__c
                 WHERE Id IN :gauIds]
            );

        for (Id gauId : gauIds) {
            if (!gauMap.containsKey(gauId)) {
                throw new AllocationException('GAU not found: ' + gauId);
            }
            if (!gauMap.get(gauId).npsp__Active__c) {
                throw new AllocationException(
                    'GAU "' + gauMap.get(gauId).Name + '" is inactive and cannot receive allocations.'
                );
            }
        }

        // --- DML: replace existing allocations ---

        // Delete all current GAU allocations on this opportunity
        List<npsp__Allocation__c> existingAllocations = [
            SELECT Id
            FROM npsp__Allocation__c
            WHERE npsp__Opportunity__c = :opportunityId
        ];

        if (!existingAllocations.isEmpty()) {
            delete existingAllocations;
        }

        // Build new allocation records using Percent so that NPSP's
        // built-in recalculation keeps Amount in sync when the
        // Opportunity Amount changes later.
        List<npsp__Allocation__c> newAllocations = new List<npsp__Allocation__c>();
        for (Id gauId : percentByGauId.keySet()) {
            newAllocations.add(
                new npsp__Allocation__c(
                    npsp__Opportunity__c          = opportunityId,
                    npsp__General_Accounting_Unit__c = gauId,
                    npsp__Percent__c             = percentByGauId.get(gauId)
                )
            );
        }

        insert newAllocations;

        return newAllocations;
    }
}
```

**Key design decisions:**

| Concern | How it's handled |
|---|---|
| **Amount stays correct after Opportunity edit** | Only `npsp__Percent__c` is set on each allocation. NPSP's own trigger logic computes `npsp__Amount__c = Opportunity.Amount × Percent / 100` on insert, and recalculates it whenever the Opportunity Amount changes — no extra code needed. |
| **Validate before mutating** | All null/empty, zero/negative, > 100 %, and inactive-GAU checks happen *before* the `delete` / `insert`. If any check fails, no DML has been issued. |
| **Replace semantics** | A SOQL query fetches every existing `npsp__Allocation__c` for the Opportunity, they are deleted in a single `delete`, then the new set is inserted in a single `insert`. |
| **Bulk-safe within one call** | The method handles one Opportunity at a time (the natural unit for a gift-entry screen). The SOQL is bounded by the map size; the DML statements are single-statement bulk calls. |

