## Analysis

The key challenge is the recursive trigger caused by `TA_Opportunity_RoundAmount` (Order 20) performing a DML update on the same opportunities. This re-fires the trigger, and our action (Order 10) would run again. TAF's `TriggerBase.idToNumberOfTimesSeenAfterUpdate` tracks how many times each record Id has appeared in the after-update context within the current transaction. On the first pass it's 1; on the second (caused by rounding DML) it's 2. We gate task creation on `timesSeen <= 1` to guarantee at most one task per opportunity per transaction.

Bulk-safety: we build a single `List<Task>` and issue one `insert` call, handling up to 200 rows comfortably.

